{"agent":"fleet-ci-help","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"The docstring claims `option_headings` rewrites \"every pre-3.13 ``-m MSG, --message MSG`` heading\", but the metavar group is `\\S+`, so any action whose args string contains a space is silently left alone and the 3.12-vs-3.13 mismatch it is supposed to erase survives. Concrete input: for a normal argparse option declared `add_argument('-f', '--file', nargs='*')`, Python 3.11/3.12 `_format_args` returns `[FILE ...]`, and `_format_action_invocation` repeats it per option string, so the help listing contains:\n\n    options:\n      -f [FILE ...], --file [FILE ...]  input files\n\nwhile Python 3.13 prints:\n\n    options:\n      -f, --file [FILE ...]  input files\n\n`_OPT_HEADING` cannot match the first line (after `-f `, `\\S+` cannot reach past the space inside `[FILE ...]`), so `option_headings` returns it unchanged; the 3.13 line is unchanged too (no space after `-f`), so `argparse_stable(actual_312) != argparse_stable(snapshot_313)` and the golden help test still fails on 3.11/3.12 for any subcommand carrying such an option — exactly the version skew this change exists to remove. The same happens for `nargs='+'` (`FILE [FILE ...]`), `nargs=2` with a tuple metavar (`A B`), and for an action whose option strings are declared long-form-first (`add_argument('--message', '-m')` → `--message MESSAGE, -m MESSAGE`), because group 2 hard-codes the short form as the first token. The new unit test only exercises metavars without whitespace (`MESSAGE`, `[N]`), so it passes while the gap stays.","digest":"34698efcaf712a73","location":"tests/pin_norm.py:36 `_OPT_HEADING` / `option_headings`","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/pin_norm.py:36 `_OPT_HEADING` / `option_headings`"}],"chunks_total":1,"coverage":"1/1 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":3336,"diff_sha":"070f0f8b492f8a7ddc554f8ff5f869090e9241241a8040d989cb280531ef6e1a","diff_source":"m